  - Y2 AC coefficient scaled by `y2ac` (only two Y columns affected, opposite signs);
  - per-segment quantizer selection via `segmentId` (same token, different segment → 129 vs 131);
  - chroma DC/AC coefficients scaled by `uvdc`/`uvac` (including the exact 131/129/127/126 AC block);
  - clamping to 255 and to 0;
  - prediction-mode equivalence classes: V_PRED (127), H_PRED (129), TM_PRED (129), and DC prediction averaging real reconstructed neighbours (200/100 → 150).
- **`B_PRED` branch**: Y2 never dequantized (`diff == null`), per-block Y1 quantizers, reconstruction feeding back into intra prediction of neighbouring blocks (128 in the first row, 130/129 propagation afterwards), chroma reconstruction, and clamping.

